From: Jeremy Melanson <1080872+zish@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 21:53:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat: let the spike's gate drop the vault's key, as a lock
 does

`--ez drop true` drops the browser's key from memory, as a lock of the
vault does, and leaves the vault open, so that the profile's keys are
locked in Gecko the way a lock locks them (encriox, stage 2's
second round); the gate's next start reads the key again, which unlocks
them. The G6's vault, once locked by the spike, did not open again with
the passphrase on file (W5), so no other phone's is locked to measure
this.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../java/org/mozilla/fenix/encri/EncriGateActivity.kt     | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/encri/EncriGateActivity.kt b/mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/encri/EncriGateActivity.kt
index 7cf6eedbe9..c9948c2bed 100644
--- a/mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/encri/EncriGateActivity.kt
+++ b/mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/encri/EncriGateActivity.kt
@@ -62,6 +62,9 @@ import org.mozilla.fenix.settings.downloads.DownloadLocationManager
  *   Every status it passes through is logged, then `fetch settled`;
  * - `--ez list true` logs what the vault holds of the two;
  * - `--ez lock true` locks the vault, for every app and for encri;
+ * - `--ez drop true` drops the vault's key from memory, as a lock of the vault does, and leaves the vault open, so that
+ *   [EncriProfileSecret.follow] locks Gecko's keys as at a lock; the next start of the gate reads the key again, which
+ *   unlocks them. It is for a phone whose vault might not open again once locked, as the G6's did not (W5);
  * - `--es login <text>` saves a login under the spike's own origin, `--es card <digits>` a card in the spike's name,
  *   and `--ez kept true` logs what the stores hold of the two, whose keys the vault's key seals (W6); `--ez forget
  *   true` deletes them. With `--ez early true`, the logins are first asked for before the vault is open, and when
@@ -143,6 +146,11 @@ class EncriGateActivity : ComponentActivity() {
             }
             extras.getBoolean("list") -> work.launch { list(context) }
             extras.getBoolean("lock") -> work.launch { lock(context) }
+            extras.getBoolean("drop") ->
+                work.launch {
+                    EncriKey.forget()
+                    Log.i(TAG, "key dropped")
+                }
             extras.containsKey("profile") -> profile(context, extras.getString("profile").orEmpty())
             extras.containsKey("login") -> work.launch { keepLogin(context, extras.getString("login").orEmpty()) }
             extras.containsKey("card") -> work.launch { keepCard(context, extras.getString("card").orEmpty()) }
-- 
